# Rich text — CKEditor via RichTextEditor

Article bodies, course summaries, and lesson summaries in admin forms use **`RichTextEditor`**, not `<textarea>`.

## Component

- [`resources/js/components/Admin/RichTextEditor.vue`](resources/js/components/Admin/RichTextEditor.vue)
- Config: [`resources/js/config/ckeditorConfigs.js`](resources/js/config/ckeditorConfigs.js)

## Variants

| `variant` | Use for |
|-----------|---------|
| `full` | Lesson article `content` |
| `minimal` | Course / lesson `summary` |

## Example

```vue
import RichTextEditor from '@/components/Admin/RichTextEditor.vue';

<RichTextEditor
    v-model="form.content"
    variant="full"
    label="Article body"
    hint="Shown to enrolled students."
/>
```

HTML is stored as-is in the database. Sanitize on public display in Phase 2+ if needed.
